2. THIRD-PARTY CORPUS DATA AND DATASETS

This category covers scripture texts, ancient source texts, translations,
lexica, morphological and linguistic annotations, and any other dataset that
Scriptura ingests from external sources.

As of milestone M0, NO third-party corpus data is present in this repository.
No datasets have been downloaded, vendored, committed, or derived. This
statement is machine-checked by tools/check_repo.py and
tests/test_repo_hygiene.py.

When datasets are added in later milestones, this section MUST be updated to
record, for each dataset, at minimum:

  * dataset identifier and human-readable name
  * upstream rights holder and copyright statement
  * exact licence name and version (or "public domain" with jurisdiction note)
  * the canonical upstream URL actually used
  * the retrieval date and the cryptographic hash of the retrieved artefact
  * the verbatim attribution string required by the licence, if any
  * whether derivatives and commercial use are permitted
  * whether the licence is share-alike and what it therefore obliges Scriptura
    to do

The authoritative machine-readable record for that information is
docs/data/licence-manifest.json. This NOTICE file carries the human-readable
attribution strings that the licences require to travel with redistributions.

Licensing for corpus data is dataset-specific. There is no blanket licence for
"the Bible", for "ancient Near Eastern texts", or for any aggregator platform.
Several upstream sources that Scriptura intends to evaluate are explicitly
licensed per item rather than per collection, so an aggregator-level licence
never suffices. Scriptura must resolve the licence of every individual item
before that item is ingested.

Where an upstream licence is share-alike (for example CC BY-SA), Scriptura
derivative datasets inherit that licence and are NOT relicensed under Apache
2.0. Where an upstream licence is non-commercial (for example CC BY-NC), the
affected dataset must be quarantined from any commercial distribution channel
and marked accordingly in the manifest.

