3. THIRD-PARTY SOFTWARE DEPENDENCIES

As of milestone M0 the Scriptura runtime has ZERO mandatory third-party
Python dependencies. The package depends only on the Python standard library
and on SQLite as provided by the platform. This is a deliberate architectural
decision recorded in docs/architecture/ADR/ADR-0002-stdlib-only-m0-runtime.md.

Optional components, each of which must be explicitly installed by the
operator and each of which remains governed by its own upstream licence, are:

  * LEANN (PyPI: leann) - optional semantic retrieval adapter, MIT License.
    Scriptura imports it behind a capability guard and degrades to SQLite FTS5
    when it is absent. See docs/architecture/BKB-ARCH-001 and
    src/scriptura/retrieval/leann_adapter.py.
  * FastAPI (PyPI: fastapi) - optional HTTP surface, MIT License. Adopted only
    behind an approved Architecture Decision Record. See
    docs/architecture/ADR/ADR-0004-fastapi-adoption-gate.md.
  * Development and CI tooling declared in pyproject.toml optional extras
    (pytest, ruff, mypy). These are development-time only and are not
    distributed with the runtime package.

When a dependency becomes mandatory, its licence must be recorded here and its
compatibility with Apache 2.0 must be assessed in an Architecture Decision
Record before adoption.


